From 71c579daeb70cc72ca97a5add498bb45d64de232 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:22:28 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] client: fix AltiVec sound mixer on VSX, stereo and loud
 sounds

The AltiVec path of S_PaintChannelFrom16 was wrong in several ways:

- On VSX targets (every ppc64le build, and big-endian -mcpu=power8+)
  plain vector dereferences compile to unaligned loads, so the
  vec_lvsl alignment trick shuffled the wrong samples. Use
  vec_xl/vec_xst there, which also need no aligned output, or
  vec_vsx_ld/vec_vsx_st on older compilers that lack them.
- On classic VMX the second source block was carried over as the first
  block of the next iteration, but with an aligned source both loads
  hit the same block and the carry went stale. Load both blocks on
  every iteration.
- The vector loop reads mono samples only, but stereo sounds were sent
  to it too.
- The vector loop multiplies by the volume as a signed 16-bit value,
  which overflows for loud sounds (channel volume * snd_vol can reach
  255 * 255).
- paintbuffer only had 4-byte alignment, so the alignment loop could
  mix the whole buffer in scalar code and never reach the vector path,
  which is what hid the bugs above. Align it to 16 bytes, which is all
  the VMX stores need.

S_PaintChannelFrom16 now only sends mono sounds without doppler
resampling and with volumes that fit to the AltiVec mixer, and
everything else to the scalar one. That leaves the stereo and doppler
code in the AltiVec mixer unused, so it is removed.
---
 src/client/snd_mix.c | 316 ++++++++++++++++++++-----------------------
 1 file changed, 150 insertions(+), 166 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/client/snd_mix.c b/src/client/snd_mix.c
index cc7c1e17d..ddc0f0cfe 100644
--- a/src/client/snd_mix.c
+++ b/src/client/snd_mix.c
@@ -38,8 +38,14 @@
 #if idppc_altivec && !defined(__APPLE__)
 #include <altivec.h>
 #endif
+// older compilers have VSX but only the vec_vsx_* names for unaligned access
+#if defined(__VSX__) && !defined(vec_xl)
+#define vec_xl vec_vsx_ld
+#define vec_xst vec_vsx_st
+#endif
 
-static portable_samplepair_t paintbuffer[PAINTBUFFER_SIZE];
+// the AltiVec mixer only takes its vector path on 16-byte aligned output
+static portable_samplepair_t paintbuffer[PAINTBUFFER_SIZE] QALIGN(16);
 static int                   snd_vol;
 
 int   *snd_p;
@@ -261,6 +267,7 @@ CHANNEL MIXING
 #if idppc_altivec
